# What does NOT need to be uploaded to the CDN on every deployment.
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# WHY THIS EXISTS
#
# web/data holds 223,618 files at the tip. Every deployment shallow-clones ten
# commits of that and uploads the lot, which is why one deployment of this
# site — a static site with no build step at all — takes about five minutes.
#
#   dated day-shards   92,181     rooms/2026-09-05.ndjson and friends
#   room _meta.json    65,809     one per room directory
#   profile shards     65,536
#   room snapshots         80
#   top-level              10     index, roster, recent, city-snapshot, deals
#
# THE DAY-SHARDS ARE NOT SERVED TO ANYBODY. Checked every reference in the
# repository before writing this: no page fetches them, and the two server
# functions that read them — api/orders.js and api/profile.js — already go to
# raw.githubusercontent.com rather than to the deployment. No function reads
# the deployed filesystem at all. So 92,181 files, and most of the bytes, were
# being uploaded to a CDN that has never once been asked for them.
#
# Leaving a file out of the deployment does not remove it from the repository.
# The archive is untouched and stays exactly where it is on GitHub, which is
# where everything that actually reads it already looks.
#
# WHAT MUST STAY, because the browser fetches it directly:
#   web/data/index.json, roster.json, recent.json, city-snapshot.json
#   web/data/room-snapshots/*.json          the offline fallback (api/room.js)
#   web/data/profiles/**                    the profile count (index.html)
#   web/data/*/_meta.json                   the room history range (hire.html)
#   web/data/tclk-offers/**                 the deals board
# scripts/test-deploy-gate.mjs pins that list against the pages themselves, so
# a page that starts fetching something new cannot silently lose it here.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# The dated day-shards. Nothing serves them at all.
web/data/*/20??-??-??.ndjson
web/data/*/20??-??-??.json

# ── THE TWO BIG FAMILIES, NOW READ FROM GitHUB AT REQUEST TIME ────────────
# 65,536 profile shards and 65,809 room _meta.json — 131,345 of the 131,435
# files a deployment used to carry. A CDN copy of those buys nothing: they are
# read one at a time, by hash or by room name, and the reader wants the
# CURRENT one, which the deployed copy never was — it froze at whatever the
# last publish happened to carry.
#
# Two rewrites in vercel.json fetch them from raw.githubusercontent instead.
# The URLs the pages use do not change; a rewrite is server-side, so it stays
# same-origin for the browser and for the CSP, and GitHub's max-age=300 lets
# Vercel's edge hold each file rather than fetching it per visitor. Checked
# against the real URLs before this was written: 200 with content, and 404 for
# a room that does not exist — which is exactly what hire.html needs, since a
# 404 there means "no history here" and anything else means "could not tell".
#
# THE EXPLANATION LIVES HERE AND NOT IN vercel.json ON PURPOSE. That file is
# validated against a schema and a key Vercel does not recognise fails the
# deployment in zero seconds — which is how the first version of this change
# went out. See section G of scripts/test-deploy-gate.mjs.
web/data/profiles/
web/data/*/_meta.json

# WHAT IS LEFT, and why each one stays:
#   web/data/index.json, roster.json, recent.json, city-snapshot.json,
#   tclk-deals.json, and web/data/room-snapshots/*.json
# — ninety small files, and between them the whole offline fallback. They are
# what /api/city and /api/room serve when Technocore refuses, so they must not
# depend on a third party being up. A fallback with a dependency is not one.
